{
  "__comment__": "The default ImSwitch2 setup: a hardware-free point-scanning microscope with one camera and one APD, everything simulated. The camera (AVManager mock) shows a live widefield image; the APD (counter-input detector on a SIMULATED NIDAQ, nidaq.simulation = true) images a synthetic sample of cells and beads from the galvo waveforms (mockSample), driven by the SimplePointScan panel: an overview (Size slider, default 60 um), a region drawn in the viewer, pixel size and dwell sliders, and three gated lasers in channels; the Advanced scan panel is one switch away. X/Y are galvo-like smooth axes reaching 100 um (5 um/V over +-10 V, vel_max 0.1 um/us, acc_max 1e-4 um/us^2); Z is a piezo-like stepped axis. To use real hardware, pick or edit another setup (Pick hardware setup...).",
